  "raw": {
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/DEB43C3FD051B594AA4F4829C8587DC3/jobs/179741": {
      "title": "Athletic Trainer",
      "description": "Athletic Trainer You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Athletic Trainer Hot Job Cumberland University - Lebanon, TN 37087 Apply Overview Level Experienced Position Type Athletics Education Level Bachelor's Degree Category Education Apply Description CUMBERLAND UNIVERSITY POSITION TITLE:  Athletic Trainer DEPARTMENT:      Athletics Department SUPERVISOR:         Associate Head AT, Head AT, and/or Director of AT GENERAL JOB FUNCTION To assist in the planning, organization, coordination, and management of the Athletic Training Department.  To assist in the management and delivery of athletic healthcare to the intercollegiate student-athletes. STANDARD EXPECTATIONS To possess the understanding of and the commitment to the University Mission. To be responsible for assisting in the development of policies and procedures for athletic training students. To be responsible for clinical instruction and supervision of athletic training students. To be responsible for assisting in the operation of the athletic training facilities. To be responsible for overseeing programs for the prevention, evaluation, treatment, and rehabilitation of athletic injuries. To be responsible for coverage of athletic teams as assigned by the Director of Athletic Training and / or Head Athletic Trainer. To be responsible for traveling with assigned athletic teams. To be responsible for assisting in the management of the athletic accident insurance program. To perform other duties/tasks as may be assigned and/or requested by the Director of Athletic Training, Head Athletic Trainer, and/or Associate Head Athletic Trainer DECISION MAKING AND MANAGEMENT On a regular and continuous basis exercises administrative judgment and assumes responsibility for decisions, consequences, and results having an impact on people, costs, and/or quality of service within the department/division. Position directly supervises athletic training students. EDUCATION AND EXPERIENCE Required:        Bachelor’s Degree in Athletic Training or related field; BOC certification; Athletic Training Licensure by the state of Tennessee, CPR/AED certification (Professional Rescuer or Healthcare Provider) Preferred:        Master’s Degree in Athletic Training or related field Experience:     0-2 years of related, collegiate level experience preferred QUALIFICATIONS AND SKILLS Communication Skills using the spoken word Proven experience in athletic training at the collegiate level Organizational Skills and the ability to prioritize responsibilities Multi-task oriented Interpersonal and Supervisory Skills Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
