    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/DEB43C3FD051B594AA4F4829C8587DC3/jobs/173029": {
      "title": "Entry-Level Librarian",
      "description": "Entry-Level Librarian You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Entry-Level Librarian Hot Job Cumberland University - Lebanon, TN 37087 Apply Overview Position Type Faculty Apply Description Position Title: Entry-Level Librarian Department: Vise Library Supervisor: Director of the Vise Library FLSA Status: Exempt The entry-level librarian position is a professional librarian position responsible for supporting the organization, accessibility, and discoverability of library resources while providing instructional services to students, faculty, and staff. This position combines cataloging responsibilities, including public service duties such as library instruction, research assistance, and scheduled circulation desk coverage. The ideal candidate will possess a strong attention to detail, excellent organizational and communication skills, and a willingness to learn and grow within an academic library environment. Training will be provided, but candidates with Master's degree from an ALA-accredited college or university in Library and Information Science. Essential Duties and Responsibilities Cataloging Perform original and copy cataloging of print, electronic, and multimedia library materials using accepted cataloging standards (MARC, RDA, AACR2, and Library of Congress subject headings). Maintain and update bibliographic and authority records in the library management system. Assist with collection maintenance projects, including inventory, withdrawals, and record cleanup. Library Instruction Provide library instruction sessions to support information literacy initiatives for students and faculty. Develop instructional materials, guides, and tutorials to support library services and research. Offer reference and research assistance in person, via email, and online. Requirement MINIMUM EDUCATION AND/OR EXPERIENCE: Master’s degree in library science (MLS/MLIS) from an ALA-accredited program, or completion expected within six months. Why Join Our Library Team? This is an excellent opportunity for an early-career librarian seeking hands-on experience in both technical and public services. We are committed to mentoring and professional development and welcome candidates who are eager to learn, collaborate, and contribute to a supportive academic environment. Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/DEB43C3FD051B594AA4F4829C8587DC3/jobs/168618": {
      "title": "Medical/Surgical Specialty Faculty",
      "description": "Medical/Surgical Specialty Faculty You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Medical/Surgical Specialty Faculty Hot Job Cumberland University - Lebanon, TN 37087 Apply Overview Education Level Master's Degree Apply Description Position Title Medical/Surgical Specialty Faculty Position Requirements 37.5 hours per week Candidate is expected to teach 24 – 30 credit hours per academic year in addition to other responsibilities (12 – 15 credit hour academic workload per semester) Posting Date Open Until Filled Closing Date Open Until Filled Job Type Full Time Faculty - 9 month teaching appointment Position Details This position is a full-time, on-ground appointment in the Rudy School of Nursing and Health Professions. The position includes teaching in both the classroom and lab environment, along with helping to coordinate clinicals. The candidate will be expected to participate in university and community service. Candidate will be required to maintain moderate engagement in scholarly and service commitments outside of the regular teaching appointment. Internal Job Category Faculty Knowledge, Skills and Abilities Faculty member must (have): Expertise in Medical/Surgical Nursing The ability to teach cognitive, affective, and psychomotor skills required by acute care nursing. The ability to operate high-fidelity mannikins, or willingness to learn Ability to work independently while adhering to high expectations and academic standards for teaching Fluency or ability to learn a variety of educational software programs Ability to provide student support and guidance for registration and advising to ensure the academic success of students Serve on committees and workgroups for the university and school of nursing Competency-based education knowledge Excellent professional communications skills Excellent oral, written and listening skills Experience The successful applicant will have: 2 – 5 years minimum in clinical setting, preferably medical/surgical nursing experience is current or very recent 1-3 years of experience teaching in an academic or equivalent educational setting such as clinical teaching in healthcare settings is preferred Strong clinical nursing skills in medical/surgical nursing Experience teaching in a hybrid environment is helpful but not required Ability to provide diverse instructional strategies including simulation Qualifications Unencumbered TN Nursing license Education Required : MSN Preferred : DNP/PhD Additional Information Requires excellence in teaching, scholarship and service Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
