    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/DEB43C3FD051B594AA4F4829C8587DC3/jobs/62566": {
      "title": "Master of Science in Athletic Training Program Third Faculty",
      "description": "Master of Science in Athletic Training Program Third Faculty You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Master of Science in Athletic Training Program Third Faculty Hot Job Rudy School of Nursing and Health Professions - TN Apply Overview Level Experienced Job Shift Full Time Education Level Doctorate Category Education Apply Description CUMBERLAND UNIVERSITY POSITION TITLE:           Master of Science in Athletic Training Program Third Faculty DEPARTMENT:                 Rudy School of Nursing and Health Profession SUPERVISOR:                   Program Director, Athletic Training GENERAL JOB FUNCTION The MSAT Program Third Faculty functions as an integral part of the MSAT Program. S/He serves as full time faculty and assists in the planning, organization, coordination, and management of the MSAT Program. STANDARD EXPECTATIONS To possess an understanding of and commitment to the University Mission. To be responsible for assisting the MSAT Program Director with development and implementation of policies and procedures for athletic training students. To be responsible for assisting the MSAT Program Director with the development and coordination of curriculum for students in the Athletic Training Program. To be responsible for instruction of MSAT curriculum. To be responsible for clinical instruction and supervision of athletic training students. To assist the CCE in recruiting strategies for prospective athletic training students to Cumberland University’s MSAT Program. To assist the CCE in marketing the MSAT Program to target audiences within the healthcare community to enhance its visibility. To assist in the development of overall objectives, determining short- and long- range goals; planning and implementing strategies to achieve goals for the MSAT Program. To oversee the Athletic Training Student Association (ATSA). To evaluate the effectiveness of services provided, and in collaboration with MSAT Program Director and faculty, devise techniques and methods of implementation consistent with national trends in the deliverance of overall athletic training student education. To ensure that the MSAT Program maintains its accreditation status by maintaining compliance and staying current with the standards and protocols set forth by the Commission on Accreditation of Athletic Training Education. To collaborate with the MSAT Program Director on creating a network of healthcare providers willing to provide their services and expertise to the education of the athletic training students. To maintain professional competence through participation in continuing education programs. To provide PRN coverage for the Department of Athletics as needed for clinical supervision of MSAT students. To perform other duties/tasks as may be assigned and/or requested by the MSAT Program Director. DECISION MAKING AND MANAGEMENT On a regular and continuous basis exercises administrative judgment and assumes responsibility for decisions, consequences, and results having an impact on people, costs, and/or quality of service within the AT Program and/or the Rudy School of Nursing and Health Professions. Position directly supervises Preceptors and athletic training students. EDUCATION AND EXPERIENCE Required : Terminal Degree in Athletic Training or related field ; BOC certification; Athletic Training Licensure by the state of Tennessee or eligible, CPR/AED Certification Professional Rescuer or Healthcare Provider) Preferred : Record of activity in national, regional, and state professional associations. CPR/AED Instructor Certified (AHA or ARC) Experience: Three – Five years of related experience required, at the collegiate level, O ne – three years of experience teaching/involvement within a CAATE accredited program. QUALIFICATIONS AND SKILLS Communication Skills using the spoken word. Proven experience in athletic training at the collegiate level. Organizational Skills and the ability to prioritize responsibilities. Multi-task oriented. Computer Knowledge. Interpersonal and Supervisory Skills. Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
